\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Optical circuit response is an upshifted cosine. The two exemplary operating points refer to the circuit being at rest, yielding the maximum possible intensity in $(0, P_0)$ and a circuit subjected to rotation, at non--zero phase shift and decreased intensity in $(\Delta \phi , P(\Delta \phi ))$.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:response}{{2}{2}{}{}{}}
