\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Modulator with a dedicated analog gain stage. MCU/DSP outputs a fixed--scale digital waveform, which directly drives a DAC with $n$--bit resolution. Then, before reaching the electro--optic actuator, the scale factor is applied by a programmable gain amplifier (PGA), or a custom analog gain stage, driven with $m$--bit word. The resulting waveform is scale--adjusted. }}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
